# **How the repository works.** Four `make` commands drive the benchmark, drawn in the diagram below. In the workbench a teammate picks a graph and a noise profile, builds a circuit, sees it written and compiled, and saves it as a circuit file; this notebook's circuit views come from it. Every input is a YAML file checked against a schema, so every result traces to a config file, a seed and pinned package versions, all in the repository at its `{{ tag }}` tag, [https://github.com/{{ repo }}/tree/{{ tag }}](https://github.com/{{ repo }}/tree/{{ tag }}).
#
# | Command | What it does |
# |---|---|
# | `make workbench` | A teammate's own workbench notebook: build a circuit and save it |
# | `make benchmark` | Makes a benchmark's runs, each recording its commit and seeds |
# | `make run` | Remakes a recorded run and reports any difference |
# | `make submission` | Renders this notebook from the recorded runs |
