# - **Why:** on hardware a qubit decays while it waits, so a fair run counts its waiting time.
# - **Why as late as possible:** a qubit then waits in |0⟩, which decay leaves unchanged, instead of waiting while it holds part of the pair. Every run is scheduled the same way.
# - **Output:** the ZZ circuit's duration and how many delays fill its idle time.

